            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="COL08" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename/>
                        <surname>Cole</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Husband of <persName key="HOL01">Thomas Holcroft's</persName> daughter Sophie (marr. c. 1794). Cole was a merchant
    in Exeter, but seems to have transferred his business to Hamburg by 1799 so that Holcroft and
    his family stay with them briefly when they first arrive in Hamburg.</p>
                        <p>Godwin's contacts with Cole are entirely at Holcrofts, save for a few entries in 1802 and 1814; but the 1830 entry is
    linked to the <persName key="KEN01">Kenneys</persName>.  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"> Thomas Holcroft, <title>The life of Thomas Holcroft, continued by William Hazlitt</title>, ed. by Elbridge Colby, 2 vols (London: Constable and Co., 1925), p. 40 and p. 285.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
